# API configuration.
#
# Copy to api/.env and fill in. Values are never committed (CLAUDE.md, Secrets).
# The application refuses to start on a missing or implausible value rather than
# falling back to a default that would be wrong in production.

NODE_ENV=
PORT=

# postgresql://user:password@host:5432/database
DATABASE_URL=

# The database `npm test` uses. It is TRUNCATED before every case, so it must not
# be the one DATABASE_URL names once that holds anything you want to keep.
#
# Leave it empty and the suite falls back to DATABASE_URL, which is what CI does:
# there the database is created for the run and thrown away after it, so there is
# nothing to lose. On a development machine there is — the leadership-tree spine
# takes an import and an adjudication to reload, and `npm test` is routine.
#
# This exists because the suite destroyed a loaded spine: thirty Persons, both
# Network roots and the only Admin account, truncated by a test run against the
# one database that served the application, the import and the tests alike.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=

# At least 32 characters, from a cryptographically secure source.
JWT_SECRET=

# Comma-separated browser origins. Empty permits none, which is correct for an
# API whose other two clients are phones.
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# The two Senior Pastors SKILL.md section 4 names, by Person id, comma-separated.
#
# Read from here and never from the database, so that who holds the role does not
# depend on a row somebody could edit (SKILL.md section 7). Not a secret — it is
# two identifiers — but it decides authority, so treat a change to it as one.
#
# Leave empty until the initial import has created them. While it is empty — unset
# or blank — no SENIOR_PASTOR account can be provisioned and an existing role row
# grants nothing, which is correct before the import and wrong afterwards.
#
# Empty aside, anything that does not name one or two distinct Person ids stops the
# process rather than failing quietly — and that includes a value which is present
# and names nobody: a lone comma is what a template renders for an empty list, and
# it looks configured. Leave it genuinely empty to mean "not yet".
#
# Read once, when the process starts. Setting it — and any later succession —
# takes effect on the next restart, so a running API will not pick it up.
SENIOR_PASTOR_PERSON_IDS=
